PDF skill for DeepSeek Harness

This package is a clean-room reimplementation of the capability set offered by
the ZCode built-in "pdf" plugin. No upstream text, script, template, or asset is
copied: the ZCode plugin and its skill are proprietary (see its LICENSE.txt),
so only the workflow structure and capability boundary were used as a
specification. Every file here is original work under the MIT license in
LICENSE.

Upstream reference (read-only, not redistributed):
  /Applications/ZCode.app/Contents/Resources/glm/packages/pdf-plugin
    .zcode-plugin/plugin.json   name=pdf, version=0.1.7, license=proprietary,
                                author=Z.ai
    skills/pdf/                 upstream routes: report, creative, academic,
                                process

Differences from the upstream plugin, and why:

- The Report route renders a Markdown subset with ReportLab instead of the
  upstream template engine.
- The Creative route prints HTML with the Chromium already required by the
  browser-use plugin, instead of a separate poster pipeline.
- The Academic route compiles the user's own LaTeX source with Tectonic and
  never substitutes another engine.
- The conversion route uses the bundled @deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit, the same
  engine DSH's office skills use, instead of a system LibreOffice.
- The process route keeps pypdf, pdfplumber, and PyMuPDF for structure,
  tables, images, and page rendering.
